// ADR 0070 / register D44: a `Fn<T,R>`-typed STRUCT FIELD. A `Fn` value is a bare
// function pointer, so the Pass-0 aggregate must be `%Struct.0 = type { ptr, i64 }`.
//
// `scg`'s `ll_type_to` — the Pass-0 field renderer — had no `cg_is_fn` arm (nor
// `cg_is_process` / `cg_is_sealed_channel`) while its own header claimed it "Mirrors
// `cgo_ty`'s mapping exactly". The field fell through to the trailing `i64`, giving
// `%Struct.0 = type { i64, i64 }` and an `insertvalue` `llvm-as` rejects with
// "insertvalue operand and field disagree in type".
//
// ⚠ THE TWO MODULES ARE THE SAME LENGTH — measured on THIS program, 534 bytes for the
// oracle, for pre-fix `scg` and for post-fix `scg` alike. A byte-COUNT check sees
// nothing here. This is a pin only because the codegen differential does a
// byte-COMPARE, and it is worth knowing that the two are not interchangeable when
// triaging a sweep.
//
// The oracle accepts this program, so the divergence was differentially LIVE and merely
// unreached: no corpus program had ever put a `Fn` in a struct field. That is the whole
// reason this file exists — the exit code below would be 42 either way, because
// `snc build` goes through inkwell, which was always right.
//
// 40 + 2 = 42.
fn inc(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 1 }

struct Holder { f: Fn<i64, i64>, n: i64 }

fn main() -> i64 {
    let h: Holder = Holder { f: inc, n: 40 };
    h.n + 2
}
